 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+### 2Q Eviction Policy
+
+The cache uses the **2Q** replacement algorithm to isolate one-off screening scans from repeatedly viewed comparison sheets:
+
+- **First-use queue (`A1in`, FIFO)**: Newly rendered sheets are admitted here. A cache hit on an entry in `A1in` serves the JPEG without promoting the entry; `A1in` remains strictly FIFO so a single screening pass cannot displace the hot working set.
+- **Ghost history (`A1out`, FIFO)**: When an entry is evicted from `A1in`, its cache key (without JPEG bytes) is recorded in `A1out` up to a bounded key capacity. When a key in `A1out` is requested and re-rendered, it is recognized as a repeat access and admitted directly into `Am`.
+- **Reused queue (`Am`, LRU)**: Holds sheets that have been accessed again after leaving `A1in`. Cache hits in `Am` move the entry to the most-recently-used position.
+
+Budgeting and eviction:
+- The 12 GiB byte limit applies to the combined JPEG data across `A1in` and `Am`. `A1in` is assigned a target byte share (25% of the 12 GiB budget, i.e., 3 GiB, tunable via worker configuration), with `Am` holding the remaining 9 GiB.
+- Before admitting a newly rendered sheet, if total cached JPEG bytes would exceed 12 GiB, evict entries until sufficient space is available: evict from the tail of `A1in` while `A1in` exceeds its target share (recording evicted keys in `A1out`), and otherwise evict from the least-recently-used tail of `Am`.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q (`A1in` FIFO + `A1out` ghost FIFO + `Am` LRU) | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets from eviction during long sequential screenings without the aging lag across project switches. Accepts extra queue bookkeeping and a configurable `A1in`/`Am` size split, all contained privately within the preview worker. |
+
